# Right-clicks are press-and-hold here (the DSL's click is the left button).
# Coordinates: TESSERA-TEST 1920x1080, scale 1, the default Control Center layout
# (setup below resets it). Material grid: x0 1512, y0 50, columns 94 apart
# (86 wide), rows 80 apart (72 tall). Glass grid: x0 1560, y0 50, columns
# and rows 82.5 apart (72.5). Default layout rows: 0 Wi-Fi 2x1 + Now Playing
# 2x2; 1 Bluetooth, Night Light; 2 Focus 2x1, Stages, Dark Mode; 3 Display;
# 4 Sound; 5 Screenshot, Record, Caffeine, Clipboard; 6 Mirroring 2x1.
look material
setup python3 -I -c "import json,os;p=os.path.expanduser('~/.config/tessera/config.json');c=json.load(open(p));c.setdefault('controlCenter',{})['layout']=[];json.dump(c,open(p,'w'),indent=4)"
wait 2
rec open 1.5 ipc panels open controlCenter TESSERA-TEST
note tiles rise in one after another from top-left, slight overshoot; compare tools/anim-timing.py with the QML recording (±1 frame)
wait 1
rec close 1 ipc panels close
note every tile stays full size while the panel fades (154 ms); longest frame gap ≤ QML's
wait 1
rec reopen 1.5 ipc panels open controlCenter TESSERA-TEST
note tiles rise in again (not already in place)
ipc panels close
wait 0.05
ipc panels open controlCenter TESSERA-TEST
wait 1
shot quick-reopen
note no invisible tiles
ipc panels close
